      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for finding this! I\u0027ve realized the changes made in patchset 2 actually broke the viewer since the hashCode() implementation wasn\u0027t consistent so the viewer couldn\u0027t find the item anymore.\n\nI think the correct way forward here is removing the faulty hashCode()/equals() implementations altogether and thus ensure that the viewer\u0027s hashmap optimization works correctly. What I don\u0027t understand though is why PlanElement.hashCode()/equals() implementations existed in the first place? As far as I can tell, hashCode() for this type has never been called anywhere and equals() was only relevant for List.indexOf() but this would work equally well with identity equality. \n\n@matthias.sohn@sap.com Do you have more information on this? Was this relevant at some earlier point?",
